From 102fc2c7032d72c62b8218fbca117e74d1a12c9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 15:49:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(libcodb): SQL identifier injection + source-bounded
 strncpy

- cosql_utils.c: the diag query "content" column list and the SUM/AVG
  column_name reach SELECT/SUM/AVG as raw SQL identifiers. is_valid_text
  permits ()%|,= and spaces, so an identifier like "1),(SELECT ..." gets
  through (post-auth admin data exfiltration). Add a strict identifier
  check ([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*) on the SELECT projection columns and on
  cosql_{sum,avg}_{between_time,latest_count_limit} column_name.
- codb_utils.c: replace the six strncpy(dst,src,strlen(src)) backup-path
  copies (source-length bounded, no NUL terminator) with dest-bounded
  snprintf.

Round-3 audit Tier C8/D9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
